    <!-- Over the cap: an imported or downgraded vault, which is a supported state because import is
         never charged against the cap. Deliberately NOT a fraction. "9 of 7" reads correctly on the
         add sheet, where the reader was refused a second ago, but in a Settings row with no refusal
         in view it implies a deficit the quota invariant denies — nothing is hidden and nothing is
         lost. So the count is stated, the keeping is stated, and the cap is described as what it
         actually limits: creating. The "one" item is unreachable (over-cap means held > cap >= 1,
         so held >= 2) and exists only because a plurals element must carry it. -->
    <!-- SECURITY-COPY: tier F -->
    <plurals name="settings_pro_row_over_cap_files">
        <item quantity="one">Files &amp; media — %1$d saved, all kept. The free version creates up to %2$d.</item>
