         TierGClaimsTest, and a fr/de/es/pt translation, and the markers and the values-*/ files
         moved together as this comment required. This paragraph said the marker was deliberately
         withheld and the group was English-only until 2026-09-21, which stopped being true when the
         translations landed — a comment describing the opposite of the file it heads, on the one
         group whose whole point is that a reviewer can tell tagged from untagged.

         Three strings here carry no marker on purpose: settings_hidden_view_entry,
         settings_hidden_peek_empty and settings_hidden_peek_taken name a control, the absence of a
         preview and a capture time, and make no claim about what concealment protects.
         settings_hidden_peek_reprompt is the one exception in that run — it explains why a screen
         lock prompt will appear, which is the re-authentication tier rather than this group's.

         Nothing in this group may carry a count or a state word on the Settings row itself: the row
         is always present, and a summary that changed with what is hidden would be the leak the
         always-present row exists to avoid.
